LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 3)
# Example 6.2 (T* = 1.20) -- liquid-vapor slab of the Lennard-Jones fluid (reduced units), interface normal along x
# usage:  lmp -in in.slab                      (run inside the folder T<value>/; T is set below)
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

variable        T       index 1.20
variable        seed    index 20251
variable        rcut    index 4.0
variable        Tmelt   index 1.0       # melt the lattice below T_c so that the slab stays intact
variable        nmelt   index 5000
variable        nequil  index 1000000
variable        nprod   index 2000000    # 1e4 reduced time units after 5e3 tau of equilibration

# 23 x 5 x 5 fcc cells at rho* = 0.746 -> box 40.3 x 8.75 x 8.75 sigma; liquid slab = 12 cells (21 sigma)
lattice         fcc 0.746
Lattice spacing in x,y,z = 1.7502781 1.7502781 1.7502781
region          box  block 0 23 0 5 0 5 units lattice
create_box      1 box
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (40.256396 8.7513904 8.7513904)
  4 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
region          slab block 5 17 0 5 0 5 units lattice
create_atoms    1 region slab
Created 1250 atoms
  using lattice units in orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (40.256396 8.7513904 8.7513904)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.000 seconds
mass            1 1.0

pair_style      lj/cut ${rcut}
pair_style      lj/cut 4.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
pair_modify     shift yes            # no tail corrections: the density is inhomogeneous (Sec. 4.6.2)
neighbor        0.3 bin
timestep        0.005

velocity        all create ${Tmelt} ${seed} dist gaussian
velocity        all create 1.0 ${seed} dist gaussian
velocity        all create 1.0 20251 dist gaussian
fix             melt all nvt temp ${Tmelt} ${Tmelt} 0.5
fix             melt all nvt temp 1.0 ${Tmelt} 0.5
fix             melt all nvt temp 1.0 1.0 0.5
thermo          1000
run             ${nmelt}
run             5000
Generated 0 of 0 mixed pair_coeff terms from geometric mixing rule
